1
00:00:00,175 --> 00:00:06,662
Teacher Guide - Writing exam questions, step by step · for teachers and Research Officers

2
00:00:06,712 --> 00:00:12,933
Welcome! In this video you will learn everything a teacher does in the SKANS Question Bank.

3
00:00:12,983 --> 00:00:19,771
We will sign in, write every type of question, add tables and answers, and send questions for review.

4
00:00:19,821 --> 00:00:26,325
Research Officers use exactly the same screens, so this video is for you too. Let us begin.

5
00:00:26,383 --> 00:00:29,950
Chapter 1: Signing in for the first time

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,506
Open the link you received. Type the username the administrator gave you.

7
00:00:36,556 --> 00:00:42,080
Now type the temporary password from the administrator.

8
00:00:42,130 --> 00:00:48,732
Not sure what you typed? Click the eye icon to show the password.

9
00:00:48,782 --> 00:00:57,406
Click the eye again to hide it. Then click Sign in.

10
00:00:57,456 --> 00:01:05,962
The first time, the system asks you to choose your own password. Type the temporary password here.

11
00:01:06,012 --> 00:01:16,682
Now choose a new password: at least 10 characters, with letters and a number. Type it twice.

12
00:01:16,732 --> 00:01:23,261
Click Save password.

13
00:01:23,311 --> 00:01:29,535
Done! From now on you sign in with your own password. Never share it with anyone.

14
00:01:29,604 --> 00:01:33,185
Chapter 2: Your dashboard

15
00:01:33,235 --> 00:01:40,816
This is your dashboard, your home page. The menu on the left has two pages: Dashboard and Questions.

16
00:01:40,866 --> 00:01:47,178
The big blue card is the quickest way to write a new question.

17
00:01:47,228 --> 00:01:56,499
These four tiles count your drafts, questions waiting for review, questions returned to you, and approved questions.

18
00:01:56,549 --> 00:02:02,168
Click any tile to open that list. Below, Recent activity shows what happened last.

19
00:02:02,225 --> 00:02:07,138
Chapter 3: Starting a new question

20
00:02:07,188 --> 00:02:14,846
The question editor opens. At the top you choose the type of question. There are six types.

21
00:02:14,896 --> 00:02:20,423
MCQ: one multiple-choice question with options (a) to (d).

22
00:02:20,473 --> 00:02:26,676
MCQ set: several MCQs that belong together, numbered (i), (ii), (iii).

23
00:02:26,726 --> 00:02:32,931
True / False: one or more statements, each true or false.

24
00:02:32,981 --> 00:02:38,184
Short: a question with one written answer.

25
00:02:38,234 --> 00:02:45,203
Long: a question with sub-questions (a), (b), (c) and parts inside them.

26
00:02:45,253 --> 00:02:48,849
Case study: a scenario followed by sub-questions.

27
00:02:48,899 --> 00:03:00,129
Below the tiles: choose the subject, the difficulty, and the marks the question is worth.

28
00:03:00,179 --> 00:03:08,739
The Title is a short name for the question. The reviewer sees it in lists, so make it clear.

29
00:03:08,804 --> 00:03:12,373
Chapter 4: Writing an MCQ

30
00:03:12,423 --> 00:03:29,253
Click the MCQ tile, give the question a title and set the marks.

31
00:03:29,303 --> 00:03:38,097
Type the question in the Question box.

32
00:03:38,147 --> 00:03:56,359
Now type the four options, (a) to (d).

33
00:03:56,409 --> 00:04:04,493
Mark the correct answer: click the round button next to it. The correct option turns green.

34
00:04:04,544 --> 00:04:15,588
Need a fifth option? Click Option. Up to six options are allowed. The bin icon removes an option.

35
00:04:15,638 --> 00:04:24,876
Print layout decides how the options are printed: one per line, in two columns or in four. Auto chooses for you.

36
00:04:24,926 --> 00:04:37,712
Further down is the Answer key. Explain why the answer is correct. This prints only in the answer key, never on the question paper.

37
00:04:37,762 --> 00:04:45,314
The question is ready. Click Submit to send it to the administrator for review.

38
00:04:45,364 --> 00:04:51,275
A green message confirms it. While a question is in review, it cannot be changed.

39
00:04:51,337 --> 00:04:54,916
Chapter 5: Writing an MCQ set

40
00:04:54,966 --> 00:05:07,735
Use an MCQ set when several MCQs share one scenario. Click the MCQ set tile.

41
00:05:07,785 --> 00:05:19,107
In the Question box, write the shared introduction for all the MCQs in the set.

42
00:05:19,157 --> 00:05:41,531
Item (i): type its question and options, and mark the correct one.

43
00:05:41,581 --> 00:06:06,531
Click MCQ to add item (ii). You can add up to forty items in one set.

44
00:06:06,581 --> 00:06:16,802
Each item has its own marks box. The total marks are added up for you automatically. Look at the bottom left.

45
00:06:16,865 --> 00:06:22,372
Chapter 6: True / False statements

46
00:06:22,422 --> 00:06:36,527
For True or False, type the statement and choose True or False as the correct answer.

47
00:06:36,577 --> 00:06:50,201
Have more statements? Click Add another statement. Each one gets its own True or False.

48
00:06:50,251 --> 00:06:58,956
Each statement is saved as its own question, so it can be reviewed and used in papers separately.

49
00:06:59,025 --> 00:07:10,266
Chapter 7: Text tools

50
00:07:10,316 --> 00:07:24,624
Above every text box is a toolbar, like in Word. Click Bold, type, then click Bold again to stop.

51
00:07:24,674 --> 00:07:32,477
Italic and Underline work the same way.

52
00:07:32,527 --> 00:07:41,933
Numbered list: click it, then choose the style. (I), (II) is used for statements like "Consider the following".

53
00:07:41,983 --> 00:07:53,270
The style buttons appear next to it: small roman (i), capital roman (I), letters (a), (A), or numbers (1).

54
00:07:53,320 --> 00:08:00,977
Press Enter twice to end the list. The alignment buttons place text left, centre or right.

55
00:08:01,051 --> 00:08:04,622
Chapter 8: Tables and amounts tables

56
00:08:04,672 --> 00:08:13,802
Amounts table inserts the usual layout: labels on the left, figures on the right under Rupees.

57
00:08:13,852 --> 00:08:30,419
Click a cell and type. The figures line up on the right automatically.

58
00:08:30,469 --> 00:08:43,434
When you are inside a table, more buttons appear: add or delete rows and columns, merge cells, header row, No border.

59
00:08:43,484 --> 00:08:52,602
The empty corner at the top left has no border, like the ICAP papers. No border can remove the lines of any cell.

60
00:08:52,652 --> 00:09:04,276
To merge cells, drag across them and click Merge. Text below starts a new line under the table.

61
00:09:04,326 --> 00:09:12,387
The normal Table button inserts a plain 3 by 3 table. The question mark button explains all table tools.

62
00:09:12,437 --> 00:09:20,090
This question is not finished yet, so click Save draft. Drafts are only visible to you.

63
00:09:20,145 --> 00:09:27,886
Chapter 9: Long questions with sub-questions

64
00:09:27,936 --> 00:09:40,019
Type the scenario in the Question box. Then write each sub-question below it.

65
00:09:40,069 --> 00:09:46,719
Each sub-question has its own marks box. Here, (a) is worth 4 marks.

66
00:09:46,769 --> 00:09:54,120
Click Sub-question to add (b).

67
00:09:54,170 --> 00:10:06,087
Inside a sub-question you can add parts: click Part (b)(i).

68
00:10:06,137 --> 00:10:14,503
The total marks are added up from the parts automatically. Numbering lets you choose (a), (i) or (1) for sub-questions.

69
00:10:14,553 --> 00:10:28,265
Under each part, click Answer to write its model answer. It prints only in the answer key.

70
00:10:28,325 --> 00:10:36,345
Chapter 10: Case studies

71
00:10:36,395 --> 00:10:53,980
A case study works like a long question: a scenario first, then sub-questions with marks.

72
00:10:54,067 --> 00:10:57,727
Chapter 11: Answer key and private notes

73
00:10:57,777 --> 00:11:04,744
Let us finish the draft from before. In Questions, choose Drafts and click Edit.

74
00:11:04,794 --> 00:11:18,798
Scroll to the Answer key. Model answer and Examiner’s advice print only in the answer key.

75
00:11:18,848 --> 00:11:30,664
Private notes are for you and the reviewer only. They never print. Use them for the source and comments.

76
00:11:30,714 --> 00:11:36,286
Click Submit when the question is complete.

77
00:11:36,358 --> 00:11:45,735
Chapter 12: The editor window

78
00:11:45,785 --> 00:11:54,051
The buttons at the top right work like Windows. Maximise makes the editor full screen.

79
00:11:54,101 --> 00:12:00,073
Restore down makes it normal size again.

80
00:12:00,123 --> 00:12:09,864
Minimise hides the editor in a bar at the bottom, so you can look at something else. Your text is kept.

81
00:12:09,914 --> 00:12:15,110
Click the bar to bring the editor back.

82
00:12:15,160 --> 00:12:21,346
Cancel or the cross closes the editor without saving.

83
00:12:21,417 --> 00:12:25,185
Chapter 13: Your questions list

84
00:12:25,235 --> 00:12:30,868
The Questions page lists your questions. Each one shows its status on the right.

85
00:12:30,918 --> 00:12:43,368
Draft: not sent yet. In review: waiting for the administrator. Returned: changes requested. Approved: ready for papers.

86
00:12:43,418 --> 00:12:53,114
Type in the search box to find questions by words in the title or text.

87
00:12:53,164 --> 00:12:59,251
You can also filter by subject and by question type.

88
00:12:59,301 --> 00:13:08,066
Click a title to preview the question exactly as written.

89
00:13:08,147 --> 00:13:11,720
Chapter 14: Duplicate and the recycle bin

90
00:13:11,770 --> 00:13:19,294
Duplicate makes a copy as a new draft. It is handy for writing a similar question.

91
00:13:19,345 --> 00:13:29,643
The bin icon moves a question to the Recycle bin. Approved questions cannot be deleted by teachers.

92
00:13:29,693 --> 00:13:34,917
Open the Recycle bin to see deleted questions.

93
00:13:34,967 --> 00:13:43,096
Restore brings a question back. Delete permanently removes it for ever. It cannot be undone.

94
00:13:43,146 --> 00:13:49,838
You are always asked to confirm.

95
00:13:49,894 --> 00:13:53,560
Chapter 15: When a question is returned

96
00:13:53,610 --> 00:14:00,606
Sometimes the reviewer asks for changes. The tile Returned to me shows how many.

97
00:14:00,656 --> 00:14:09,404
The reviewer’s comment is shown under the question in red. Read it, then click Edit.

98
00:14:09,454 --> 00:14:35,073
The comment is also shown at the top of the editor. Make the change...

99
00:14:35,123 --> 00:14:42,272
...and click Submit again. The question goes back to the reviewer.

100
00:14:42,343 --> 00:14:46,002
Chapter 16: Your account

101
00:14:46,052 --> 00:14:53,847
At the bottom left you see your name. The key icon changes your password at any time.

102
00:14:53,897 --> 00:15:03,780
Type your current password and the new one twice, then Save password. Forgot your password? Ask the administrator.

103
00:15:03,830 --> 00:15:10,302
When you finish, click the sign-out icon, especially on a shared computer.

104
00:15:10,352 --> 00:15:17,325
You are ready to write questions - Questions? Ask your administrator. Thank you for helping build the SKANS Question Bank.
